{"authored" [{"question" "q-70969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $T(7,0,-3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $T$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70969" "f