56" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 23 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-12,21,-4⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-13,33,-14⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33819" "field" "selection" "