 "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $E(16,-1,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,-7,2⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩$ and $r=⟨15,2,-3⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨5,1,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,11,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $E(16,-1,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $e=⟨16,-1,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =e+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨1,11,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨16,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verif