"basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "463337ec68298752e57b253f36ce61dc23deb2b60c656593886ee6b3c0850fb4" "basis" 1507 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value