or of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-3i-7j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-33822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-33822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-33822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-3,-7,-8⟩"] ["math" "⟨-3,13,-8⟩"] ["math" "⟨-5,1,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨13,3,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,1,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-33822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-3,-7,-8⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $w=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-5,3,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-5,3,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-1,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,2,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,-3,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-5,3,1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,7,-2⟩+t⟨-3,4,1⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩$ and $w=⟨5,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-9i-j-23k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-19,-1,17⟩"] ["math" "⟨-7,-3,-23⟩"] ["math" "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩"] ["math" "⟨-9,1,-13⟩"] ["math" "⟨-9,3,-21⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨2,-7,3⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,-2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨3,6,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-3,2⟩+s⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨7,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502ceb