allel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-128499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-128499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and $r=⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,2,-3⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨-1,0,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-70976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_