(16,-1,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $e=⟨16,-1,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =e+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨1,11,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨16,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨9,-7,2⟩+t⟨15,2,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨5,1,-2⟩+s⟨16,-1,3⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "The plane is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-70978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-71034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $L(-1,-1,1),\\,M(2,5,-3)$, and $N(0,-8,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-71034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =⟨2,5,-3⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =⟨0,-8,-1⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $l=⟨-1,-1,1⟩$ of the point $l,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =l+s\\overset{\\to }{LM}+t\\overset{\\to }{LN} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/state.json" "file_sha256" "d526e2393a1241fb2502cebde1d4789dafbd406b3bdda2fe62cfc9e3da8b67a7"} {"question" "q-71034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bac8017a7b1f2806a0606b007b551ced5b2fcb760a3ff30eee3030fcbab782b0"} {"question" "q-71034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/ja